# Everything text is LF in the repo and in the working tree, on every OS: the files at the top and in each folder,
# but plugin/. The Claude plugin directory wants a plugin's files checked out exactly as committed, with no rule in
# here touching them. ponytail: a line a folder; a new top-level folder needs its own line to be LF on Windows.
/* text=auto eol=lf
/.claude/** text=auto eol=lf
/.claude-plugin/** text=auto eol=lf
/.cursor-plugin/** text=auto eol=lf
/.github/** text=auto eol=lf
/examples/** text=auto eol=lf
/fonts/** text=auto eol=lf
/scripts/** text=auto eol=lf
/skills/** text=auto eol=lf
/src/** text=auto eol=lf
/templates/** text=auto eol=lf
/test/** text=auto eol=lf

# Pictures and models are binary. (PNGs too, by their bytes: no rule, so none touches the plugin's icon.)
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.heic binary
*.pdf binary
*.glb binary
*.ttf binary
*.webp binary
